Z||000006||Fierobruiser||12-24-2001||12:39 AM||||I just passed a dark blue (not factory blue) GT that I've never seen before in Emmaus on my way to Allentown around 2:30 today. He didn't even return my wave. Don't Fiero drivers wave when they pass? In the 60's and 70's, sports cars always waved at each other because there weren't very many of us. It always seems that Fiero drivers never acknowledge other Fieros. Has that tradition become uncool?<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||12-24-2001||12:56 AM||||I was driving a friend's red 86 GT and looked across the intersection and saw a very familiar car coming toward me. I thought, "Bob's car is looking good today" but then realized that I was in Bob's car. A very attractive young lady in a identical red GT locked eyes and grinned really big as she waved in passing. So, then I thought "was it me...or the car. Dammit, it was the car."||||reg||1
Z||000008||grgoyl86||12-24-2001||08:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierobruiser:<BR><B>I just passed a dark blue (not factory blue) GT that I've never seen before in Emmaus on my way to Allentown around 2:30 today. He didn't even return my wave. Don't Fiero drivers wave when they pass? In the 60's and 70's, sports cars always waved at each other because there weren't very many of us. It always seems that Fiero drivers never acknowledge other Fieros. Has that tradition become uncool?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We always wave. Sometimes the other car waves, and looks perplexed as to why we waved. Sometimes they wave back and think it's cool. One day my wife waved at a young "lady" driving a twin to hers, and the other driver gave her the finger!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <BR>Some people just don't get it! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">||||reg||1
